; Workspace-wide build environment.
;
; In the `release` profile, set FENNEC_DROP_TESTS so the fennec test ppx strips every inline-test
; body (let%test / let%test_unit / let%prop / executable doctests) down to `let () = ()`. That keeps
; the shipped binary lean — it links none of the test runtime (Fennec_hunt_unit / Fennec_hunt_prop)
; or its deps (qcheck-core). The dev profile leaves tests in place, so `dune runtest` and
; `fennec test` run them all. (env-vars are part of each action's environment, so dune rebuilds
; correctly when the profile changes.)

(env
 (release
  (env-vars
   (FENNEC_DROP_TESTS true)))
 ; `fennec dev` builds under this custom profile = dev minus `-g`. The bytecode link of the SSR server
 ; otherwise re-serializes the debug section of the WHOLE image (opam + fennec + frontend) on every
 ; edit — ~180ms, the dominant cost of an incremental rebuild. Dropping `-g` makes the link ~7x faster.
 ; `fennec dev --debug` uses the standard `dev` profile to restore line-numbered backtraces.
 ;
 ; CRITICAL: dune only auto-enables js_of_ocaml SEPARATE compilation in the built-in `dev` profile; a
 ; custom profile silently falls back to WHOLE-PROGRAM jsoo, which re-translates the entire client image
 ; (runtime + every lib + app) on every edit (~0.64s here vs ~0.28s incremental — and the client bundle
 ; is the long pole of `@dev`). So we must force `separate` back on, or the -g win is more than erased.
 (fastdev
  (ocamlc_flags
   (:standard \ -g))
  (js_of_ocaml
   (compilation_mode separate))))
